WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.067 --> 00:00:03.406
- [Voiceover] The backwards baseball cap.

00:00:03.406 --> 00:00:04.476
The sunglasses.

00:00:04.476 --> 00:00:05.535
The punny name.

00:00:05.535 --> 00:00:09.702
This is Lou Seal, mascot for
the San Francisco Giants.

00:00:14.814 --> 00:00:16.678
Before they had Lou, the
Giants did something,

00:00:16.678 --> 00:00:18.058
well, a little crazy.

00:00:18.058 --> 00:00:20.180
It was 1984 and the
Giants weren't just bad,

00:00:20.180 --> 00:00:21.429
they were awful.

00:00:21.429 --> 00:00:22.806
To offset the team's losing streak,

00:00:22.806 --> 00:00:25.317
they created an
anti-mascot, the Crazy Crab,

00:00:25.317 --> 00:00:27.691
so fans would have something
other than the team to hate.

00:00:27.691 --> 00:00:28.889
And it actually worked.

00:00:28.889 --> 00:00:30.251
But the love/hate relationship

00:00:30.251 --> 00:00:32.845
quickly turned into a
hate/hate relationship.

00:00:32.845 --> 00:00:34.117
Things got out of hand.

00:00:34.117 --> 00:00:35.774
The fans and even players started throwing

00:00:35.774 --> 00:00:37.257
things at the Crazy Crab.

00:00:37.257 --> 00:00:38.831
Due to safety issues, the Giants pulled

00:00:38.831 --> 00:00:41.831
the Crazy Crab anti-mascot for good.

00:00:42.806 --> 00:00:46.236
This is where the lovable
anti-anti-mascot comes in.

00:00:46.236 --> 00:00:47.976
Lou Seal was born on Farallon Island.

00:00:47.976 --> 00:00:50.635
He's a bay area native and one cool dude.

00:00:50.635 --> 00:00:52.812
He's universally beloved
and a crowd favorite.

00:00:52.812 --> 00:00:54.142
A far cry from the anti-mascot

00:00:54.142 --> 00:00:56.559
formerly known as Crazy Crab.

